  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="DA">From Margins to Mainstream</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="DA">The vision of the programme is to ensure that persons with intellectual disabilities and their families are fully and meaningfully included in society and recognized as citizens with equal access and treatment. Through empowerment activities and organisational development, families are mobilised, persons with intellectual disabilities gain self-confidence and competencies to actively participate in their local communities and engage as self-advocates and the capacity of partner organisations is strengthened to deliver long-term, impactful change. Through awareness-raising and advocacy, the programme will foster long-term inclusion as communities learn to understand and accept; service providers provide better support; and policies are influenced to promote inclusion of persons with intellectual disabilities and their families.</narrative>
  </description>
